# Clean, reusable components

Write clean, well-structured code with reusable components.

- One component does one job. A page composes sections; a section composes smaller pieces.
- Extract anything used twice (markup, logic, or constants) into a shared component, hook, or named constant.
- Keep props small and explicit. Do not pass unused data through a component.
- Name files and components for what they render (`CourseCard`, `PartnerStrip`), and put them in the feature folder that owns them.

```jsx
// Bad: one component owns the title, the list, and the card markup
function Courses({ courses }) {
  return courses.map((course) => (
    <article key={course.id}>
      <h3>{course.title}</h3>
      <p>{course.priceLabel}</p>
    </article>
  ));
}

// Good: the list composes a reusable card
function CourseList({ courses }) {
  return courses.map((course) => <CourseCard key={course.id} course={course} />);
}
```
